    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • The Volkswagen Group's Affordable BEV Quartet Has Almost Reached 150,000 Orders\nXPENG Reveals G9L at the 2026 Paris Motor Show, Dubbed As the Ultimate \"Large SUV for the AI Era\"\n34 photos\nPhoto: XPeng\nGuangzhou Xiaopeng Motors Technology, commonly known as XPENG , was established less than a decade and a half ago, but it's already a major player at the 2026 Paris Motor Show in France.\nXPENG (also noted as Xpeng) was born in 2014 in Guangzhou, China, but already has offices in Mountain View, California, and Munich, Germany, and trades publicly on both the New York Stock Exchange and the Hong Kong Stock Exchange. The company sees itself as the purveyor of a Physical AI ecosystem spanning technology stacks, humanoid robots , flying cars, and AI-defined vehicles, including the L03, P7+, G6, G9, and X9.\nThe company is currently making a major appearance at the 2026 Paris Motor Show from October 12 through 18 at the Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, “bringing its latest advances in intelligent mobility, robotics and future transportation to one of Europe’s most prominent automotive stages.” Most importantly, the company has announced the global launch of its next-gen AI flagship SUV, the XPENG G9L, “marking another milestone in the company’s expansion in Europe.”\nThe stand at the Mondial de l’Auto has the theme of an immersive “Physical AI Museum” spanning four areas: the brand’s technology stack, AI-defined vehicles, humanoid robots, and flying cars. Of course, the new G9L took center stage, and XPENG has already announced that it will introduce the new flagship SUV to other regions, too, like Australia and New Zealand, without also providing the launch timing, pricing, or specifications.\nOver on the Old Continent, the XPENG G9L has the XPENG NGP - Next Generation Pilot, which is the company’s next-generation intelligent driving technology, powered by a second-generation VLA model and a high-computing-power AI architecture. The VLA 2.0 will provide both city and highway assisted driving, navigation-based assisted driving, and more. XPENG intends to roll out the NGP in 2027, and the G9L also introduces XPENG’s Kunpeng Super Electric REEV technology: it combines a large battery, fast charging, efficient EV drive, and intelligent energy management.\nMore precisely, the XPENG G9L will have up to 287 km (WLTP) or 178 miles of EV range thanks to the REEV version featuring a large 63 kWh LFP battery pack, while the range extender system provides “long-distance flexibility when required” and extends the combined range to up to 1,200 km (WLTP) or 746 miles. Just like other REEVs (or EREVs), the G9L is driven by the electric motors in all conditions, and there’s a combined output of 430 kW or 577 hp and 695 Nm (513 lb-ft) of torque.\nThe company says the vehicle has no less than 24 energy-flow optimization strategies, but it’s still capable of hitting 62 mph or 100 kph in just 5.4 seconds, and the 1.5-liter turbocharged engine is relegated to working in the background, with XPENG targeting a difference of less than one dB between their Super Electric REEV and pure-electric operation under test conditions.\nBy the way, there will be a regular EV model, too, packing the same 430 kW or 577 hp and 695 Nm (513 lb-ft) of torque but sans the 1.5L turbo and with a larger 110-kWh battery pack that provides a rating of up to 553 km of WLTP range, or 344 miles. The model also has a DC fast-charging rating of up to 540 kW, so the 10-80% recharge would take less than 12 minutes at a suitable DC ultra-fast charging station.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nXPENG G9L Xpeng G9L Australia Paris Motor Show 2026 Paris Motor Show Mondial de l'Auto 2026 Paris Motor Show\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Aurel Niculescu\nAurel has aimed high all his life (literally, at 16 he was flying gliders all by himself) so in 2006 he switched careers and got hired as a writer at his favorite magazine. Since then, his work has been published both by print and online outlets, most recently right here, on autoevolution. Full profile\nUP NEXT 1970 Hemi Cuda With 4.10 Rear Is Full of Questions, Comes With $250K Auction Price Set in 2015",
